{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15006-battlestar-galactica","id":15006,"title":"Battlestar Galactica","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-20T17:33:31-08:00","id":15006,"title":"Battlestar Galactica","content":"It's not just me, right? Humanoid Cylons are essentially Angels minus some of the more overt powers. I can even relate number models to Incarnations.<br /> Season 4 Spoilers<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Seems like Rebel Cylons work pretty well as Demons, the Final Five to an extent as well. God/Gaius and God/Six seem like ascended Qashmallim also.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T18:24:36-08:00","id":15025,"title":"","content":"What you call God/Gaius and God/Six are actually angels, as per the end of the show, they also work quite well as GMC style Angels. Starbuck is also an Angel by the end of the show, though one that believes she is the person whose identity she has assumed (her Cover) until her mission is accomplished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T18:40:56-08:00","id":15036,"title":"","content":"Good call on Starbuck, for Gaius and Six I figured Qashmallim worked since the God Machine in Battlestar would be bext characterised as... well, a lie. John's fabricated version of the One God worshipped by the Centurions after he disposed of the Final Five.<br /> The... Being(?) that the Qashmallim operate for is a more compassionate force as far as I'd read it, and so more suited to the God that acts through Starbuck and Gaius and Caprica Six.<br /> <br /> It could also be the God Machine though. A God Machine dedicated enitely to either maintaining or disrupting the cycle. Honestly I just made the post because I was straight up flabbergasted NOT to see BSG listed in the References, but then I just finished the series so *Shrug*<br /> Maybe I'm seeing it everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1247-maseiken","name":"Maseiken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1247_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T04:12:40-08:00","id":15292,"title":"","content":"the God-Machine in the core WoD book is significantly more benevolent than the one presented in GMC and Demon. it could be that the God-Machine has changed, that its dealings are shrouded in lies and propaganda, or that it is capable of both benevolence and cosmic evils depending on the circumstances.<br /> ...which all in all sounds like something a complex, unknowable God would be.<br /> <br /> And the God-Machine maintaining a cycle of things that have happened before and will happen again, yet seemingly improves with each iteration sounds <i>exactly</i> like something from GMC. A loop of operations that eventually will push reality into its next phase.<br /> <br /> As for the One God, it wasn't John that fabricated it -- the centurions already had the faith before the Final Five arrived (Anders explains as much when he tells them about Ellen's role &quot;they had a loving god, Ellen said this changed everything&quot;), John just didn't believe in it and abused it to control the other humanoid cylons.<br /> <br /> See also the spinoff Caprica for <i>elaborate</i> backstory on the One God faith. Turns out the faith predates the invention of the cylon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","user":"sikker","date":". 11-21-2013, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}